#################################################################
# DAY 5 FINAL EXERCISE: BOOKING SYSTEM API TESTING SPECIFICATION
#################################################################

### 1. Get All Bookings (Part C)
# Expected Status: 200 OK
# Expected Response: Empty array [] initially, or list of bookings.
GET http://localhost:8081/api/bookings

---

### 2. Create a Valid Booking (Part E)
# Expected Status: 201 Created
# Expected Response: Booking object with ID "BK001" and status "CONFIRMED"
# Business Impact: Will reduce EV001 available seats from 120 to 118 (Part H)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "EV001",
  "participantName": "Rahim Gonzalez",
  "participantEmail": "rahim@example.com",
  "seats": 2
}

---

### 3. Get One Specific Booking by ID (Part D)
# Expected Status: 200 OK
# Expected Response: The booking record details for BK001 matching Test 2
GET http://localhost:8081/api/bookings/BK001

---

### 4. Create a Booking with Missing/Invalid Fields (Part B Validation)
# Expected Status: 400 Bad Request
# Expected Response: Error array flagging that "seats" must be greater than 0
POST http://localhost:8081/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "EV001",
  "participantName": "Rahim Gonzalez",
  "participantEmail": "rahim@example.com",
  "seats": 0
}

---

### 5. Create a Booking with an Invalid Event ID (Part F Validation)
# Expected Status: 404 Not Found
# Expected Response: {"message": "Event EV999 was not found"}
POST http://localhost:8081/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "EV999",
  "participantName": "Rahim Gonzalez",
  "participantEmail": "rahim@example.com",
  "seats": 2
}

---

### 6. Create a Booking with Too Many Seats (Part G Capacity Validation)
# Expected Status: 400 Bad Request
# Expected Response: {"message": "Not enough seats available"}
# Context: EV002 only has 35 seats available from bootup
POST http://localhost:8081/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "EV002",
  "participantName": "Rahim Gonzalez",
  "participantEmail": "rahim@example.com",
  "seats": 100
}

---

### 7. Optional Task: Cancel Booking via DELETE
# Expected Status: 200 OK
# Expected Response: Booking details showing status updated to "CANCELLED"
# Business Impact: Restores the 2 seats back to event EV001 stock count
DELETE http://localhost:8081/api/bookings/BK001